# CT9/CT0 AC-ANALYTICS: screen/section context values diverge from the ticket's own documented table

## module_switched (CT9) — from Categories app bar
Logging event: origin=app,name=module_switched,params=Bundle[{to_module=Pharmacy, screen=home,
source=categories_app_bar, from_module=Grocery & Food, position=2, from_module_id=1, to_module_id=3,
section=module_tabs}]

Documented (ticket AC-ANALYTICS table): screen=categories, section=app_bar
Actual: screen=home, section=module_tabs
Root cause: ModuleController.switchModule() (module_controller.dart ~line 1176-1180) hardcodes
'screen': 'home', 'section': 'module_tabs' unconditionally; only `source` was made call-site
configurable.

## select_item (CT0/CT10)
analytics: select_item {item_id: 49166, screen: category_screen, item_list_id: category_items,
item_list_name: category_items, index: 0, store_id: 3291, category_id: 8}

Documented: screen=categories, item_list_id=category_grid
Actual: screen=category_screen, item_list_id=category_items
Root cause: category_screen.dart:472-476 (NEARS-3632's own new code, CT0 fix-cycle 1) constructs
  AnalyticsContext(screen: 'category_screen', section: 'category_items', position: index + 1)
instead of the ticket's own documented screen=categories / section=category_grid values.

